Sanitize TypeBounds in @retains arguments to the top capability

Namer#inferredResultType applies `deskolemized` to inferred result types; on a
type whose capture set holds a skolem (a dependent method applied to an
unstable argument), the ApproximatingTypeMap maps the skolem element to a
range, `derivedOrType` merges it with neighbouring elements, and
`derivedAppliedType` re-packs the range as a wildcard argument of @retains.
A TypeBounds is not a legal capability: it crashed the pickler before 3.9
("no TypeBounds allowed") and now surfaces as "Illegal capture reference"
when the annotation is forced, e.g. for the export forwarder of a transparent
inline method (Soundness #1410). Capture sets are covariant and the range's
upper bound has absorbed the surviving refs, so approximating the bounds by
`any` loses no precision, in analogy to the existing skolem case.

Developed with LLM assistance (Claude); mechanism and fix validated against a
minimal reproduction and a full Soundness build.

Enabled by `-Z:retains-bounds`; without it, upstream's code runs at every site this
patch touches.

